NNAAMMEE
     ssttddbbuuff — change standard streams initial buffering

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssttddbbuuff [--ee _b_u_f_d_e_f] [--ii _b_u_f_d_e_f] [--oo _b_u_f_d_e_f] [_c_o_m_m_a_n_d [...]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssttddbbuuff is used to change the initial buffering of standard input, stan‐
     dard output and/or standard error streams for _c_o_m_m_a_n_d.  It relies on
     libstdbuf(3) which is loaded and configured by ssttddbbuuff through environment
     variables.

     The options are as follows:

     --ee _b_u_f_d_e_f
             Set initial buffering of the standard error stream for _c_o_m_m_a_n_d as
             defined by _b_u_f_d_e_f (see _B_U_F_F_E_R _D_E_F_I_N_I_T_I_O_N).

     --ii _b_u_f_d_e_f
             Set initial buffering of the standard input stream for _c_o_m_m_a_n_d as
             defined by _b_u_f_d_e_f (see _B_U_F_F_E_R _D_E_F_I_N_I_T_I_O_N).

     --oo _b_u_f_d_e_f
             Set initial buffering of the standard output stream for _c_o_m_m_a_n_d
             as defined by _b_u_f_d_e_f (see _B_U_F_F_E_R _D_E_F_I_N_I_T_I_O_N).

BBUUFFFFEERR DDEEFFIINNIITTIIOONN
     Buffer definition is the same as in libstdbuf(3):

           "0"   unbuffered

           "L"   line buffered

           "B"   fully buffered with the default buffer size

           _s_i_z_e  fully buffered with a buffer of _s_i_z_e bytes (suffixes 'k', 'M'
                 and 'G' are accepted)

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     In the following example, the stdout stream of the awk(1) command will be
     fully buffered by default because it does not refer to a terminal.
     ssttddbbuuff is used to force it to be line-buffered so vmstat(8)'s output will
     not stall until the full buffer fills.

           # vmstat 1 | stdbuf -o L awk '$2 > 1 || $3 > 1' | cat -n

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     libstdbuf(3), setvbuf(3)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssttddbbuuff utility first appeared in FreeBSD 8.4.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The original idea of the ssttddbbuuff command comes from Padraig Brady who im‐
     plemented it in the GNU coreutils.  Jeremie Le Hen implemented it on
     FreeBSD.

